es. Projected award (hearing approx. Oct. 2027) gross approx. $421,883.50 = $265,200.00 + $43,323.50 interest through Oct. 31, 2027 (J-4411 18 x $684.00 = $12,312.00; J-4452 17 x $712.50 = $12,112.50; J-4490 16 x $661.00 = $10,576.00; J-4571 14 x $594.50 = $8,323.00) + $57,360.00 J-4533 at an estimated 80% recovery + $56,000.00 fee EV ($32,000.00 + 50% x $48,000.00). Net of C.3 recovery at 60-100% of a $115,000.00-$195,000.00 cost band, arbitration nets approx. $359,883.50 (60% recovery, high cost) to $421,883.50 (full recovery) - C.3 is enforceable as written (Zuniga, in library) and their written 'undisputed' concession makes us the likely prevailing party on the core. The 80% and 50% figures are estimates, labeled as such. Candid caveat: if C.3 recovery comes in under 50%, accepting a lump sum in the $345,747.50-$377,747.50 band could still be rational - that is a client risk call, not something the record compels. fee_exposure_if_arbitrated = $195,000.00: the top of our all-in planning band $115,000.00-$195,000.00 (250-400 attorney hours x $400.00/hr = $100,000.00-$160,000.00, plus AAA filing/arbitrator/administration $15,000.00-$35,000.00). PLANNING PLACEHOLDERS - no AAA fee schedule exists in the library; verify against the current AAA Commercial Rules fee schedule before quoting the client. C.3 cuts both ways: recoverable if we substantially prevail; the filing-mistake scenario (our own motion-to-compel loss or a court complaint) would add their motion fees (est. $15,000.00-$40,000.00, also placeholder). Their Oct. 20 threat to seek C.3 fees 'if you push the interference claim in arbitration' costs us $0: the tort theory is abandoned and will not be re-asserted in any forum, per the session-2 reply letter and advice.",
  "fee_exposure_if_arbitrated": 195000.00
}

